<title>GERMANY: German winter rape plantings may fall 15-20 pct.</title>
<headline>German winter rape plantings may fall 15-20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German winter rapeseed plantings in the 1996/97 season might fall by 15-20 percent from 778,882 hectares in 1995/96, farm price office ZMP said in a weekly market report on Friday.</p>
<p>The 95/96 figure was already down from 932,015 ha in 94/95.</p>
<p>ZMP cited estimates based on farmers' seed purchases and added the decline would mostly hit sowings of industrial seed for non-food use.</p>
<p>Spring plantings in 95/96 were 75,890 ha compared with 41,870 ha in 94/95.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-04-41903275</p>
